+# Package READMEs, screenshots and funding — results
+
+**Date:** 2026-10-13. **Branch:** `feat/package-readmes`, cut by hand from
+`main` at `51125b6` (`main` has not moved since: `git merge-base main HEAD`
+is `51125b6`). Spec:
+[2026-10-13-package-readmes-design.md](../specs/2026-10-13-package-readmes-design.md)
+(revision 1, amendments A1–A4 from planning). Plan:
+[2026-10-13-package-readmes.md](../plans/2026-10-13-package-readmes.md),
+executed task by task with an implementer and an independent reviewer per
+task. This note is the record. Its shape follows
+[2026-10-13-publish-host-packages-results.md](2026-10-13-publish-host-packages-results.md).
+
+Nothing here ran `dart pub publish` without `--dry-run`, pushed, merged or
+tagged: those are the human's (STATUS, Resume here). The merge has not
+happened, so the release checklist writes `<merge commit>` for the human to
+fill.
+
+## What this branch does
+
+The three published packages (0.7.1 on pub.dev) get what a pub.dev page
+shows: a README with images, `screenshots:` in the pubspec, `funding:`
+links, and a package table; all three go to **0.7.2**. The images are
+generated by a new unpublished package, `tool/screenshots` (flutter_test,
+real fonts, no pixel comparison). The README code is analysed in a second
+tool package, `tool/readme_probe`. Two CI scripts keep both honest:
+`check_readmes.dart` and `check_screenshots.dart`. R-10's two exports
+(`SymbolLibraryState` family, `TableNumberProblem`) go on the planner's
+barrel, which the 0.7.1 note had left as a 0.x candidate.
+
+## The controller's rulings
+
+Quoted from the SDD ledger, each with its cost if wrong.
+
+- **R1.** Task 3 keeps the `SymbolLibraryLoader` in a local the scene passes
+  to both `FloorPlanController(symbols:)` and `_ready` (the plan's own
+  fallback). Cost if wrong: none, test-only code.
+- **R2.** The renderer's barrel does not re-export `DraftDocument` /
+  `SpatialIndex`, so the renderer README's example tells the reader to add
+  both packages (`dart pub add jet_cad_2d jet_cad_2d_flutter`, as the
+  engine's says for vector_math) and the probe imports both barrels. Cost
+  if wrong: one README sentence.
+- **R3.** `check_screenshots` stays red from Task 5 to Task 8: the plan
+  orders the check before the data it checks; nothing pushes in between.
+  Cost if wrong: none (no CI run on this branch before the merge).
+- **R4.** FT2 compares the icon's ink against a tofu reference drawn in the
+  same test (the icon's codepoint in an unloaded family, which is Ahem) and
+  requires the icon's ink to be under half the reference's and above 0.02.
+  The plan's absolute bound (0.02, 0.6) passed an Ahem box (0.333), so
+  M-FT2 survived. A relative bound kills it without a threshold tuned to
+  one glyph. Cost if wrong: one test rewrite.
+- **R5.** M-SH3 becomes `if (updating)` → `if (true)` inside `shoot`. The
+  plan's variant is unreachable: SH3 returns early when `updating`. Cost if
+  wrong: none.
+- **R6.** Task 3b was inserted before Task 4: `RulerFrame` passes the
+  ambient `DefaultTextStyle`'s `fontFamily` to `RulerPainter`'s label style
+  (null family = today's style, unchanged), a test killed by named
+  mutations, the renderer's CHANGELOG 0.7.2 says so; then P1 and P2
+  regenerated. Why: D4 requires real fonts in every picture and no public
+  API reaches the rulers' labels (they drew as test-font boxes under
+  `flutter test`). On a device the ambient family is the app's own font, so
+  the rulers then match the host's text. **Cost if wrong: one small
+  published behaviour change in the renderer to revert before release; the
+  human sees it here and in "Rulings I made" before the merge.**
+- **R7.** In the renderer's gate on macOS, `text_lod_ladder` rungs 1 and 2
+  pass; this is the known macOS difference (STATUS, Owed to the human,
+  macOS), not a regression of Task 3b, which touches no ladder code. The
+  renderer's gate on this machine is judged by "only those two differ".
+  Cost if wrong: a Linux CI red at the next push, visible at once.
+
+## Two facts for the record
+
+1. **The renderer gained a code change.** The spec's original line was "no
+   code change"; R6's Task 3b (`5600f4f`) changed
+   `packages/jet_cad_2d_flutter/lib/src/ruler_frame.dart` and
+   `ruler_painter.dart` (`RulerFrame.build` also went from an expression to
+   a block body, about 145 lines of diff noise). The 0.7.2 CHANGELOG says
+   so.
+2. **The plan's Global Constraints were wrong about `SymbolWords`.** They
+   list `SymbolWords` among the names the scenes may take from
+   `package:jet_cad_floor_plan/editor.dart`; it is not exported there (nor
+   by the planner barrel; only `SymbolNames` is). The renderer scene does
+   not need it: `searchSymbols(entries, query, [SymbolWords words =
+   SymbolWords.english])` takes it as an optional parameter, and the
+   default gives `e.name` and `g.category`. The scene calls
+   `searchSymbols(library.entries, '')`. Nothing is imported from `src/`.
